Dhanlaxmi Bank Payment Gateway (PG) Integration Document 



I. Request parameters from merchant site to DhanBank 

When a customer from merchant site selects Dhanlaxmi Bank’s payment gateway, the following parameters have to be sent to Bank’s web portal through secured protocol (https) via post method. In case of UAT, the protocol would be “http” via post method (below mentioned URLs are UAT, production URL will be shared at the time of production movement).

Parameter Name	Parameter Desc	Mandatory Flag (Y/N)	Max Length	Remarks
PID	Payment Identifier of the Merchant 	Y	20	PGREFID
PRN	Payment Reference No from the Merchant Site	Y	30	Varchar2 data type 
AMT	Payment Amount	Y	14,2	Number Field
CRN	Currency Code	Y	3	Default Value INR
RU	Return URL (To be Shared by K S E B)	Y		
MN	Merchant Name	Y	50	
ACTNO	Account Number related to the CIF number	N	30	


Request parameters will be encrypted using AES.jar library and the encrypted value is assigned to ‘encDhanBankData’ variable. This ‘encDhanBankData’ will be sent to the bank using HTTPS POST method. 

Along with this ‘encDhanBankData’ request parameter, merchant should send the “mercode” request parameter with value of “PGREFID” (value equal to PID in the above)

The AES jar file and the key for encryption/decryption has to be shared by Dhanlaxmi Bank.

